## Context
Child E of tracker 1045, split from child D (1171) on 2026-10-21 at the author's
request, because it needs no gate record and removes repeated runs now. The same
checks run four or five times per head (coder, `/gaze`, the adherence seat,
`/verify-gate`, forge CI). The forge still runs `.github/workflows/CI.yml` on
every push, so a conclusion for each head already exists, even though the ruleset
`main-required-checks` was disabled on 2026-10-21 and nothing waits on it.

Known limit: a forge conclusion is for the branch head, not the merge candidate;
the candidate run is child A (1156). Known fact: with the ruleset disabled, the
merge helper merges on arming without waiting for CI (PR 1561 merged five
seconds before its last check finished), so this ticket does not make CI a gate.
It only stops `/gaze` and `/verify-gate` from repeating a result that already
exists.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `/gaze` and `/verify-gate` read the forge's check conclusions for the PR
      head commit (the exact head sha they review) and, when every job of the
      workflow is complete and green, run only a targeted test run of the files
      the diff touches instead of the full suite.
- [ ] Pending, failed, missing, or older-than-head conclusions fall back to the
      current full run; they are never read as green and never skipped. A positive
      control (green for this head: no full run) and a negative control (green
      for an older head, or pending: full run) are tested.
- [ ] The skills name the capability ("the forge's check conclusion for a
      commit"), not a tool, and require nothing of a particular agent runtime.
- [ ] The result each skill reports names what it read (workflow, head sha,
      conclusion) so the trail shows the run was not repeated and why.
- [ ] `.github/workflows/CI.yml` is not changed here (trim is child D).
- [ ] Catalog regenerated and drift check clean; PR under the 15-file breaker.
